# NTRE Reference Implementation Self-Evaluation Code and Data

This directory contains the self-evaluation code and data for the NTRE x86 reference implementation package.

It is used to support functional verification, benchmark data collection, resource measurement, and microbenchmark analysis for the NTRE reference implementation.

## Directory Layout

The current directory is organized as follows:

```text
.
├── Benchmark_Results/
├── microbenchmarks/
├── scripts/
└── README.md
```

## 1. Benchmark Results

The `Benchmark_Results/` directory stores the generated benchmark results, functional verification logs, resource measurement data, and microbenchmark summaries.

The files currently included are:

```text
Benchmark_Results/
├── ntre_auxfunc_microbench_summary.md
├── ntre_auxfunc_microbench.csv
├── ntre_auxfunc_microbench.log
├── ntre_poly_microbench_summary.md
├── ntre_poly_microbench.csv
├── ntre_poly_microbench.log
├── ntre_symmetric_microbench_summary.md
├── ntre_symmetric_microbench.csv
├── ntre_symmetric_microbench.log
├── ntruplus_ntre_fair_baseline.csv
├── x86_self_eval_functional.log
└── x86_self_eval_resource.csv
```

The main files are described below:

| File                                   | Description                                                                                            |
| -------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
| `x86_self_eval_functional.log`         | Functional verification log, including build, KAT execution, and output comparison records             |
| `x86_self_eval_resource.csv`           | Static size and process-level peak RSS measurement results                                             |
| `ntruplus_ntre_fair_baseline.csv`      | Engineering reference benchmark data comparing NTRE and the NTRU+ baseline under the same test harness |
| `ntre_poly_microbench.csv`             | Raw microbenchmark data for polynomial-arithmetic related functions                                    |
| `ntre_poly_microbench.log`             | Build and run log for polynomial microbenchmarks                                                       |
| `ntre_poly_microbench_summary.md`      | Summary of polynomial microbenchmark results                                                           |
| `ntre_symmetric_microbench.csv`        | Raw microbenchmark data for symmetric primitive related functions                                      |
| `ntre_symmetric_microbench.log`        | Build and run log for symmetric primitive microbenchmarks                                              |
| `ntre_symmetric_microbench_summary.md` | Summary of symmetric primitive microbenchmark results                                                  |
| `ntre_auxfunc_microbench.csv`          | Raw microbenchmark data for auxiliary functions                                                        |
| `ntre_auxfunc_microbench.log`          | Build and run log for auxiliary-function microbenchmarks                                               |
| `ntre_auxfunc_microbench_summary.md`   | Summary of auxiliary-function microbenchmark results                                                   |

## 2. Microbenchmark Source Code

The `microbenchmarks/` directory contains the C source files used for local function-level microbenchmarking.

```text
microbenchmarks/
├── ntre_auxfunc_microbench.c
├── ntre_poly_microbench.c
└── ntre_symmetric_microbench.c
```

The files are used as follows:

| File                          | Description                                                            |
| ----------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `ntre_poly_microbench.c`      | Microbenchmark source code for polynomial-arithmetic related functions |
| `ntre_symmetric_microbench.c` | Microbenchmark source code for symmetric primitive related functions   |
| `ntre_auxfunc_microbench.c`   | Microbenchmark source code for auxiliary functions                     |

These files are self-evaluation test code and are not part of the NTRE algorithm source implementation.

## 3. Scripts

The `scripts/` directory contains shell scripts used to run the benchmark and microbenchmark tests.

```text
scripts/
├── run_ntre_auxfunc_microbenchmarks.sh
├── run_ntre_benchmarks.sh
├── run_ntre_poly_microbenchmarks.sh
└── run_ntre_symmetric_microbenchmarks.sh
```

The scripts are used as follows:

| Script                                  | Description                                                      |
| --------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `run_ntre_benchmarks.sh`                | Runs the main NTRE benchmark and engineering reference benchmark |
| `run_ntre_poly_microbenchmarks.sh`      | Runs polynomial-arithmetic microbenchmarks                       |
| `run_ntre_symmetric_microbenchmarks.sh` | Runs symmetric primitive microbenchmarks                         |
| `run_ntre_auxfunc_microbenchmarks.sh`   | Runs auxiliary-function microbenchmarks                          |

## 4. How to Run

Run the following commands from this directory:

```sh
chmod +x scripts/*.sh
```

To run the main NTRE benchmark:

```sh
./scripts/run_ntre_benchmarks.sh
```

To run the polynomial-arithmetic microbenchmarks:

```sh
./scripts/run_ntre_poly_microbenchmarks.sh
```

To run the symmetric primitive microbenchmarks:

```sh
./scripts/run_ntre_symmetric_microbenchmarks.sh
```

To run the auxiliary-function microbenchmarks:

```sh
./scripts/run_ntre_auxfunc_microbenchmarks.sh
```

The generated results are written to the `Benchmark_Results/` directory.

## 5. Expected Output Files

After running the scripts, the following output files may be generated or updated:

```text
Benchmark_Results/ntruplus_ntre_fair_baseline.csv
Benchmark_Results/ntre_poly_microbench.csv
Benchmark_Results/ntre_poly_microbench.log
Benchmark_Results/ntre_poly_microbench_summary.md
Benchmark_Results/ntre_symmetric_microbench.csv
Benchmark_Results/ntre_symmetric_microbench.log
Benchmark_Results/ntre_symmetric_microbench_summary.md
Benchmark_Results/ntre_auxfunc_microbench.csv
Benchmark_Results/ntre_auxfunc_microbench.log
Benchmark_Results/ntre_auxfunc_microbench_summary.md
```

The functional verification and resource measurement evidence files are:

```text
Benchmark_Results/x86_self_eval_functional.log
Benchmark_Results/x86_self_eval_resource.csv
```

## 6. Reproducibility Notes

For reproducible results, it is recommended to:

1. Run the scripts on an x86-64 platform.
2. Use the same compiler and build configuration as described in the self-evaluation report.
3. Avoid running other CPU-intensive workloads during benchmarking.
4. Keep the directory structure unchanged.
5. Preserve all generated `.csv`, `.log`, and `.md` files under `Benchmark_Results/`.

The benchmark and microbenchmark data in this directory are intended to serve as reproducible technical evidence for the NTRE x86 reference implementation self-evaluation.

## 7. Notes

This README describes only the self-evaluation code and data in the reference implementation package.

The NTRE algorithm source code is provided separately in `1_算法源代码/`.

The formal self-evaluation report is provided separately as `3_自评估报告.pdf`.

The dependency statement is provided separately as `4_依赖说明.md`.
